From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: geramyloveless <gloveless@jqluv.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 19:33:01 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [Loom/AMDGPU] Let gfx12 VOPD components read an identical
 VGPR source

RDNA4 descriptor sets carry a new descriptor-set flag,
VOPD_SAME_VGPR_SOURCES. With it, the VOPD planner accepts a pair whose
components read the same 32-bit physical VGPR in the same source slot
instead of rejecting it as a bank conflict, so a shared operand (an FMA
row factor, a common subtrahend, a packed DOT2 input) no longer blocks
dual issue or forces a source swap. Other descriptor sets keep the
bank rule unchanged.

vopd_plan.loom-test covers shared-source FMAC, SUB and DOT2 pairs on
gfx1201, and the commuted-binary case now pairs without swapping.
